 `ask` is the host-rendered decision type. A live document's open block decisions appear in one compact, cycling `#b-<blockId>` navigation link beneath the tab row. There is one ask component on every surface: a decision block *hosts* the Inbox's `AskCard` (compact variant, thread collapsed, `frame="block"`) for its indexed ask row, so answering, **Ask back** (a clarification posted as a reply on the ask — `createComment` on an issue document's ask, `createArtifactComment` on a project document's — which leaves the decision open), the folded reply-count disclosure over the exchange, the question-shaped-answer prompt, the `ASK_EDITED` reload, the answered and resolved records (`AskCompletionCard`), and the retryable save error all behave exactly as they do in the Inbox, and a reply or answer made in either place shows in the other. An ask block marked `invalid`, or one with a missing question or option label, renders its raw content as a malformed decision without a card until the block text is repaired. The editor library supplies its schema-aware Insert and Turn into block-menu entries; Dispatch passes the server schema rather than duplicating those commands.
 
-A decision block is a card whose chrome is React and whose question text stays the editor's. `features/doc/ask-block.ts` mounts a ProseMirror `NodeView` for `ask` (`installAskBlockView`, merged into the library's node views right after the editor is created, in both `ProofDocument` and `VersionView`): it owns only the shell — the urgency accent and tint (`askUrgencyAccent`, `askBlockTint`, `askBlockPill` in `theme/classes.ts`), a `contenteditable="false"` header slot, the content hole, and a `contenteditable="false"` footer slot — and registers each mounted block as an `AskBlockHost` (slots + node) in React state; `update()` swaps the node and re-registers without remounting the content hole. `ignoreMutation` excludes the slots so ProseMirror never re-parses the card as an edit, and `stopEvent` keeps keystrokes in the answer controls away from the editor's keymaps. `features/doc/AskBlockCard.tsx` is the host: it portals into the two slots (the same `createPortal` pattern `MarkdownBody` uses for reference anchors) and renders nothing the card already has. The header names the block type — the urgency pill (`URGENCY_LABELS` from `features/inbox/ask-urgency.ts`) and "Decision" — and the footer is `<AskCard frame="block" variant="compact" thread="collapsed">` once the server has indexed the block into an ask row and the surface is live; `frame="block"` drops the card's own frame, urgency accent and notch, question, and block link, since the block shell draws the frame, the editor shows the question, and the block is the link's target (the card's metadata line still says who asked and when, with the `dispatch://` reference; `AskCompletionCard` takes the same `frame` and skips the question). Until the row exists, and on a read-only surface (closed issue, version view), the block reads its own attributes instead: the header adds who asked and when (from the row, if any), "Answered by … · when", and a Resolved / Closed pill, and the footer shows the options with the chosen